a28]","[#201b6]"],"edgeStrings":["[#201b6]_#_[#3ba28]","[#3ba28]_#_[#5e5b8]"],"description":"These neurons are both occasionally active, firing at random every so often. Since these are random, and the inhibitory neuron will stop the output excitatory neuron, the excitatory output will mostly be supressed. But once in a while when the inhibitory signal is quiet, SpikerBot will meow  without any input just like a cat!","thumbnail":""},{"id":"1775499453239","neuronKeys":[],"edgeStrings":["[#c5357]_#_[#a3901]","[#c5357]_#_[#13db4]"],"description":"Experiment with what objects SpikerbBot will want to play with by changing these camera inputs.","thumbnail":""}],"info":{"title":"Curious Cat","description":"Turn SpikerBot into a cat! It chases around a red object like a yarn ball, and meows at random.","author":"User","version":"1.0.1","timestamp":"2026-04-08T15:35:07.282148"}}